 bishop so maybe instead  they recognize that the next move is  going to be queen here 2h7  that's going to be checkmate and so  maybe they play something like rook 2e8  trying to give their king another place  to go  but now that rook here on f8 was  protecting  this square here on f7 white's now free  to take  on f7 this is not going to end well it's  going to end in a checkmate after king  2h8  queen comes back here to h5  king g8 queen up here h7 and then there  is a checkmate  pretty soon after that  so that was the example if they take the  bishop here on h7 it is going to end  extremely bad for them they're either  going to give up their queen  or they're going to lose the game very  quickly the only other option they have  is to play king 2h8  same thing from white they're gonna play  knight to g5 now this is not check  so they do have that going for them as  far as black not being under  immediate threat but they still have to  worry about  the queen coming here to h5 on the next  move so  if they start to look at how can black  defend against this they could think  that maybe bishop here to e7 does  something it attacks the knight here on  g5 now they have the bishop and the  queen here on  d8 but this doesn't matter too much  because  the knight takes here on f7 and this is  check  and this is also attacking the queen  here on d8 so if they decide you know  what i'm just gonna take this bishop  okay y just takes the queen and the game  is  completely lost for black once their  queen is gone  and if they don't take the bishop here  on h7  maybe they decide let's let's take that  knight here on  f7 well now queen two h5  preparing to move the bishop there will  be a discovered attack here not a lot of  great ways to protect against this  maybe knight to f6 trying to open up  something  giving up some material but after the  pawn takes here  bishop takes then bishop to g6  check king is forced to move here to g8  and after the bishop takes it's  protected by the queen here as well  king over here to f8 bishop to g6  and things are lost for black  so that was if they play bishop here to  e7 they don't have to play that they  could try something else maybe g6 all  these are going to  be bad moves there's just nowhere for  black to run after the greek give  sacrifice here on  h7 maybe pawn two g6 is an  effort here and yes that does stop the  queen coming here to h5 but everything  is so blocked off from black here you  can see  none of these pieces bishop here on c8  knight on b8  rook on a8 can really get involved into  the game  this knight here on a d7 is pretty  locked out can't come to f6 it just dies  immediately  bishop here on b4 is completely out of  the game and the queen has a hard time  getting involved into the game it can  it can try just coming here to e7  but it doesn't do a whole lot and so  white has a lot of time that even if  they don't come to queen h5  they can just come to queen to g4  knowing that the next move queen to h4  puts a lot of pressure on their opponent  and maybe they try to get their queen  involved into the game because  there's no other options here queen to  e7 can't come to queen to f6  because it just falls to the pawn here  but then  maybe just queen two h3 this is still a  discovered attack if  the bishop moves right here so maybe  they  get their king out of the way king 2g g7  but then knight 2 e4 and this is a nice  little move here because it prepares  if they ever need to uh to get the  knight up here to f6  it opens up the door for the dark script  it should get involved into the game and  the pawn can't take it right here  because that would lose the game  immediately  this bishop is protected by the queen  the queen is protected by the bishop  here on c1  this is check king comes back here to h8  and then a very quick  checkmate from here so if we come back  after the move knight to  e4 we could see  uh some other effort that's just not  going to go  extremely well like where do they  actually move here they can't come to  king 2 f6 uh they can't  come up here to h8 it's going to be a  qui pretty quick checkmate after bishop  takes here  on g6 with the discovered attack uh they  can't really get their knight involved  into the game because the pawn can take  it as well as  the knights they can always exchange  here on c3  but that's just delaying time none of  their pieces can really get involved  into the game  so white can pretty much sit back and do  whatever they want to with a very strong  attack  with the threat of queen to h6 on the  next move because remember  that is defended by the bishop here on c  one so that is the greek greek gift  sacrifice hopefully you guys enjoy this  also that  sacrifice here on age seven if you're  curious  when can white sacrifice their bishop  here on h7 and when can they not because  it's not always an option for you  sometimes it can go extremely poorly  i will have a link at the end of this  video  that will detail exactly what you should  be looking for it's a video i made a  while back but tells exactly the setup  that you should be looking at  to know when you can actually take this  pawn here on h7  and when you cannot so definitely if you  like this and you think that this is  something that may come up in your game  i highly recommend watching that video  as well it's gonna make a lot more sense  around  why this works and why you may see it  often in your games  uh so definitely check that out thank  you guys so much for watching the video  i'll see you guys next time  you

